PROGRAM: compareTrees

USAGE: compareTrees estimate.nwk reference.nwk > output.txt

DESCRIPTION: Compare two collections of phylogenetic trees representing
samples from two posterior (or other) distributions over tree space --
for example, samples from a variational approximation and from an MCMC
reference run.  Reports the mean per-split Bernoulli KL divergence between
the two samples' posterior distributions over clade splits.  For each
non-trivial clade split observed in either estimate.nwk or reference.nwk,
treats inclusion of the split as a Bernoulli variable with posterior
inclusion probability estimated from the corresponding sample, and
computes KL(p_est(s) || p_ref(s)).  The reported value is the average over
the union of splits observed in either sample (Laplace-smoothed so no
split has probability exactly 0 or 1).  This approximates the KL
divergence between the two posterior distributions over tree topology,
and remains well-behaved even when the two samples share few or no exact
topologies, unlike the full-topology KL divergence -sum p(tau) log
(p(tau)/q(tau)).  Both input files must contain one Newick tree per line,
sampled over the same set of taxa.

OPTIONS:
    --help, -h
        Print this help message and exit.
